{
  "bio": [
    "Ratmir Timashev is the cofounder and former CEO of Columbus, Ohio-based data management firm Veeam.",
    "He and his college friend Andrei Baronov cofounded Veeam in 2006 and sold it to VC firm Insight Partners for $5 billion in 2020.",
    "Before Veeam, Timashev and Baronov cofounded systems management tools outfit Aelita Software in 1996; they sold it to Quest Software for $115 million in 2004.",
    "In 2026, Timashev launched Oh.io, a VC firm that's aiming to invest $100 million to bring 100 early-stage startups to Columbus, Ohio over five years.",
    "Timashev is a major donor to his alma mater, Ohio State, giving around $150 million including a $110 million gift in 2020 to establish the Center for Software Innovation."
  ],
  "about": [
    "Timashev renounced his Russian citizenship in 2024 in opposition to the invasion of Ukraine and is now a dual American-Cypriot citizen.",
    "While working as a PhD student in Moscow in the early 1990s, Timashev fixed roofs and cleaned windows in the summer and weekends to earn more money."
  ]
}